  "id": "nes",
  "term": "NES",
  "definition": "NES refers to night eating syndrome, a pattern of eating in which a substantial amount of food is eaten after the evening meal and/or during the night while the person is aware of the eating. It is also associated with features such as reduced appetite in the morning, sleep problems, low mood later in the day, and distress or problems in functioning.",
